<!-- Community Involvement -->
<div class="section-community-wrap">
    <section id="section-community" class="community community--new community--new-top">
    {% comment %} <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/community.css"> {% endcomment %}
    <div class="page-width">
        <div class="community-intro">
            <h3>Community <br class="visible-sm" /> involvement</h3>
            <div class="community-info">
                <p>We are committed to making a positive impact within our organization and the wider community by supporting inclusion, diversity, equity, and initiatives that benefit society. These policies guide our efforts for a better world.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="community-row community-col-wrap">
            <div class="community-col">
                <h4 class="col-title">EQUITY PROGRAM</h4>
                <p>Our Induction Program provides structured learning on vital topics such as Unconscious Bias and Diversity Development. To reinforce these values, we conduct annual re-training sessions and continuous education, ensuring that our team remains engaged in fostering an inclusive, diverse, and equitable work culture. We also encourage open discussions and feedback, empowering employees to actively contribute to a more supportive and fair workplace for everyone. In addition, we provide mentorship programs and leadership training to ensure long-term inclusivity at every level of the organization.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="community-col">
                <h4 class="col-title">INDIGENOUS  RECONCILIATION  PLAN</h4>
                <p>We are actively working on our Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), with an anticipated submission in June 2024. As part of this initiative, we support Indigenous businesses such as National Dynamic Supplies and AES Aboriginal Employment Services. Additionally, we proudly showcase Indigenous artwork across our sites, symbolizing our ongoing commitment to First Nations communities. Through partnerships, education, and cultural engagement, we aim to enhance understanding, build closer ties, and foster meaningful, lasting reconciliation efforts. Our goal is to foster respect, amplify Indigenous voices, and integrate their heritage into our workplace culture.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="community-col">
                <h4 class="col-title">JASONL IS PROUD TO BE A CORPORATE MEMBER OF SUPPLY NATION.</h4>
                <p>
                    <img src="{{ 'supply-nation-member-logo1.png' | file_img_url:'100x'}}" alt="supply nation member" style="float: left; padding: 10px 20px 0px 0;">
                Supply Nation connects its members to Indigenous suppliers to build a vibrant and sustainable Indigenous business sector by incorporating Indigenous owned businesses into the supply chain of Australian companies and government agencies. Our membership as an organisation connects us further with Indigenous businesses helping them grow and continue to thrive whilst building a prosperous Indigenous-owned sector.</p>
